        "warningEmitted": false,
        "clipExtractionGatedOnSkin": true,
        "clipCountIfExtractClipsWereCalled": 1,
        "trackCountIfExtractClipsWereCalled": 0,
        "note": "The converter calls ExtractClips only for a skinned group, so with no skin the .cnj has no 'animations' key at all. Even when called, ExtractClips resolves the channel target against the joint set and skips it, producing a clip with zero tracks. Fixing this needs a real node hierarchy to animate, which is why D6 depends on the Phase 5 architecture rather than on the animation layer alone."
